From 3cf999f8fc1f403f11313c553c4bec641d5c9101 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <steven.nguyen.bn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:27:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp P4a] TR-098 WANDevice frame + common/ethernet/DSL
 objects in C

WANCommonInterfaceConfig (9), WANEthernetInterfaceConfig + Stats (8) and
WANDSLLinkConfig (5) ported from functions/tr098/wan_device: 22 parameters,
8 objects.  The WANIPConnection / WANPPPConnection instances below
WANConnectionDevice.1 stay with sdk/mtk/compat/ for now, so only the three
ported objects are claimed in .paths.

Kept verbatim from the product:
 - WANAccessType is empty -- its shell getter wan_common_get_access_type()
   is referenced once and defined nowhere in the function library.
 - WANEthernetInterfaceConfig / WANDSLLinkConfig are constants on this
   PON/Ethernet gateway, and their writable leaves accept and drop a write.
 - Boolean spelling follows the shell ("true", "1") so a value comparison
   against the old client on the board reports no false difference.

NOT BUILD-TESTED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wan_mtk.c   | 346 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wan_mtk.h   |  31 ++
 public/libs/libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/sdk.mk    |   3 +-
 3 files changed, 379 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 public/libs/libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wan_mtk.c
